            <ArticleTitle>Association of a temporomandibular disorder and Eagle's syndrome: case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>53-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a clinical case of Eagle's syndrome which required dental intervention due to the presence of exacerbated symptoms indicating an association with a temporomandibular disorder. The therapeutic dental procedures used were an occlusal splint and temporary removable partial dentures. Surgical removal of the styloid process on the left side was later performed as a medical option.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
